{"name":"Deer God","hex":"#96847a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ruminant mammal with hooves and often antlers, of the family Cervidae, or one of several similar animals from related families of the order Artiodactyla, such as the musk deer or mouse deer.","Such a mammal that is in the family Cervidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deer"},{"term":"god","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Godié."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deity or supreme being; a supernatural, typically immortal, being with superior powers, to which personhood is attributed.","An idol.\nA representation of a deity, especially a statue or statuette.\n Something or someone particularly revered, worshipped, idealized, admired and/or followed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/god"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer"},{"title":"God","blocks":[{"text":"A supreme deity, supreme being, supreme god, or simply just God, is a deity within theistic belief systems which is believed to be the ultimate cause of all things in existence. As such, it is seen as the creator, sustainer, and ruler of the universe. God is often thought of as incorporeal and independent of the material creation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg/330px-Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/1280px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACervidae_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/1280px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Stag Hunt of Frederi